avatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-27T13:08:09Z","updated_at":"2025-04-27T13:08:09Z","body":"Updated per https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105821#issuecomment-2833442705","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833451544/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833496119","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105821#issuecomment-2833496119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105821","id":2833496119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6o47g3","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-27T14:51:26Z","updated_at":"2025-04-27T14:51:26Z","body":"I think I found the culprit—\r\n\r\nLooks like there are indeed two issues with the checks that hide empty categories.\r\n\r\nFor reference, here is the section:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e37c6261ea48b1a339c469282df7e9b7c073a72f/editor/editor_inspector.cpp#L3546-L3564\r\n\r\nFirstly, although both metadata and scripts are hidden, the category checks only exclude metadata:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e37c6261ea48b1a339c469282df7e9b7c073a72f/editor/editor_inspector.cpp#L3550\r\n\r\nSo, the `script` property incorrectly allows its category (`RefCounted`) to be considered \"not empty\".\r\nThis can be fixed just by adding the check.\r\n\r\nSecondly, the loop automatically breaks at the end of the list without setting `valid = false`.\r\nThis is interpreted as having found a visible property, so the last category is always shown, even if empty.\r\n\r\nA simple null check mitigates this second issue.\r\nThis shouldn't risk any false positives, as any successful hit & `break` on a valid property guarantees a non-null iterator.\r\n\r\nThese two changes still solve the original issues (as well as making the section more correct!), so I'll update the PR with this approach.\r\n\r\nI think this is a much cleaner fix, thank you for your insight!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2833496119/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858373978","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105821#issuecomment-2858373978","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105821","id":2858373978,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6qX1Na","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-07T12:20:08Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T12:20:08Z","body":"If the inspected object is RefCounted, it does not look correctly:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e58a8922-5ffa-4f61-86a7-097e1450d1a1)\r\nAlthough normally it's not possible to edit a pure RefCounted; you can do it with EditorScript:\r\n```GDScript\r\nfunc _run() -> void:\r\n\tvar ref := RefCounted.new()\r\n\tEditorInterface.get_inspector().edit(ref)\r\n```\r\nMoreover, if you edit a RefCounted class with variables, you will get script under script category:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e001bab9-2b20-42bb-bd0c-7cee844de951)\r\nWithout this PR:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79df3970-b570-4b9b-baaa-62b06b6ea90e)\r\nBut as I said, it's not something that's normally possible, so maybe not worth worrying about.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2858373978/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939369203","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105821#issuecomment-3939369203","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105821","id":3939369203,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qzgDz","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T20:14:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T20:14:23Z","body":"Rebased to current master.\r\n\r\n> If the inspected object is RefCounted, it does not look correctly:\r\n> ...\r\n> Moreover, if you edit a RefCounted class with variables, you will get script under script category:\r\n\r\nI couldn't get the provided script to run without immediately causing a crash.\r\nRegardless, I'd agree that this is atypical enough to not worry about.\r\n\r\nThe `script` property appears under whatever the final category is (with or without this PR), so inspecting a pure `Object` already appears like in the first image.\r\n\r\nThis PR essentially just fixes the handling of the final category to allow it to be hidden if empty (ie `RefCounted`).\r\nThe already-existing behavior that places `script` somewhat awkwardly is untouched.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939369203/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]